t030o44-measure-2 run 2 (2026-10-02T08:05:13Z to 08:12:27Z, exit 0, 719 PASS, 0 FAIL), kept as run, with its script
(t030o44-measure-2-run2.sh) and candidate (t030o44-edits/kernel-3-run2.pairs). It measured an intermediate
candidate and is superseded by the run of record (t030o44-measure-2.*) for three reasons, each found after it
started by running the full suite on that candidate in a standalone copy (147 tests, test_reports_and_tally
17/18, every other suite passing) and reading every failing assertion:
1. Its item rule let any nested list item opened by a bold label (vf_field_item) stand as a line of its own. That
   both refused the 19 White_Space separators T030o43 review 2 reads (`-<U+00A0>**Class:**`, which by CommonMark is
   no list item, so the next field line looked like a continuation) and let a nested `- **Tier:** data-loss` under
   a minor Severity through. The record's item rule instead lets through only a line the pass itself reads as a
   field line of its own.
2. Its quoted-record rule refused a quoted field line outside any finding (the shipped `finding-summary` manifest
   holds a fenced `- **Severity:** minor` in a summary section). A quoted field line outside every finding
   attaches to none; the record refuses a quoted Finding heading anywhere and a quoted record line inside a
   finding.
3. Its vf_block_start did not accept the HTML blocks that may interrupt a paragraph (CommonMark 4.6 conditions
   1, 3, 4, 5), so a `<pre>` directly after a field line was refused; the record reuses the tracker's vf_raw_start.
Every history comparison of run 2 passed and holds for the record's candidate too, which the record re-measures.
